# Build-context filter for backend/Dockerfile, which is built from the repository root
# (Compose services `migrator` and `backend`). The context is an allow-list: only backend/ and
# batch/ are sent to the builder. The frontend image uses frontend/.dockerignore instead.
#
# data/ and var/ stay out on purpose: Compose mounts ./data read-only at /app/data and
# ./var/batch-output at /srv/var/batch-output at run time.
*
!backend
!batch

# Secrets and local environment files, at any depth. backend/.env holds SECRET_KEY and the
# database URLs, which reach containers only from the Compose environment at run time.
**/.env*

# Local virtual environments, bytecode, tool caches and coverage data, and the egg-info left by
# the host's editable installs. The image installs its Python dependencies from the requirements
# manifests, so it needs none of these.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/.coverage
**/*.egg-info
